    {
      "call_source": "transcript_item",
      "params_digest": "61a67cc980ae828e",
      "query": "{\"content\": \"P(grant) 0.01. The petition asks whether the PLRA's 150% cap on attorney's fees is a strict cap on awards (the \\\"greater than 150% of the judgment\\\" text in 42 U.S.C. \\u00a7 1997e(d)(2)). The respondent waived their right to respond on June 24, 2026, indicating they view the petition as weak and unlikely to be granted. There does not appear to be a deep circuit split on whether the statute prohibits awards greater than 150%; the overwhelming majority of circuits treat it as a hard c",
